  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING CHANGES:\n- SpaceWeatherNoaaClient changed from static to instance-based class\n- Now requires HttpClient injection via constructor\n- All methods changed from static to instance methods\n\nMigration guide:\n  // Before (static API)\n  var data = await SpaceWeatherNoaaClient.GetKpIndex1MinAsync();\n  \n  // After (instance-based with DI)\n  var client = new SpaceWeatherNoaaClient(httpClient);\n  var data = await client.GetKpIndex1MinAsync();\n\nCritical fixes:\n- Fix HttpRequestBase to use injected HttpClient instead of creating new instances\n- Prevents socket exhaustion by properly reusing HttpClient instances\n- Rename 'Client' property to 'HttpClient' for clarity\n\nType changes:\n- Change OvationAuroraDataItem.Probability from decimal to double\n- Add Probability01 property for normalized value (0.0-1.0)\n- Update probability calculation: Convert.ToDecimal → Convert.ToDouble\n\nArchitecture improvements:\n- Full dependency injection pattern implementation\n- Compatible with IHttpClientFactory and ASP.NET Core DI\n- Enhanced testability with mockable dependencies\n- Better lifecycle management for HttpClient\n\nBenefits:\n- Eliminates socket exhaustion issues\n- Enables proper HttpClient reuse\n- Supports advanced HTTP configuration (timeout, headers, policies)\n- Follows modern .NET best practices\n- Improves performance and resource management",
